  "context_files_formal_coverage": false,
  "review_conclusions": [
    "Static interface IDs connect typed exports, imports and slot resolution. Duplicate export checks belong to registration, while wrong Rust provider downcast may produce NotEnabled even for an entry whose published state is Enabled.",
    "An installed entry is enabled only for an even generation with a present provider sampled from the same state. A slot only identifies a position in its originating table; constructing it does not validate membership or define a native ABI layout.",
    "Disable retains a provider, deactivate removes it, and reload replaces matched owner exports while preserving a disabled generation. Transition modes name requested operations, and reports observe resulting entry state.",
    "StrongBridge owns the acquired Arc; clones retain that provider and later table replacement does not retarget existing handles. Catalog disable/deactivate guard declared strong dependents before transition; handle construction does not perform that lifecycle check.",
    "VM and native admission count before invoking the callback, so callback errors remain admitted calls. Absent slots do not count; native lease denial counts as not enabled, while missing methods do not.",
    "DefaultConfigManager accepts an in-memory update then requests background persistence. Its weak core failure is RuntimeUnavailable; get returns None for unavailable core or absent key.",
    "Flush captures a target generation and waits for confirmation. Timeout leaves the background operation live, and persistence errors do not imply in-memory rollback. A worker snapshot may contain newer values than the captured target it confirms.",
    "Report attempt and byte/latency counters include completed failures. Only successful writes advance persisted generation and clear last_error; the64 sample latency window and coalesced pending indicator describe current implementation bounds.",
    "The three owned tests assert explicit sequential entry transitions, static ID/Arc address sharing and changed-versus-unchanged notification behavior; they do not establish concurrent behavior or real disk persistence.",
    "Existing CR-PLUGIN-BOUNDARY-0001 and0002 remain open in read-only context; no new issue markers or behavior fixes are included."
  ],
